# Lane ownership — LCC (server) and RCC (client) — CLAUDE.md, V2 §5.
#
# This alone does not enforce anything: GitHub only applies CODEOWNERS review
# requirements on a repo with branch protection enabled, and this repo's plan
# does not currently permit that (`docs/FOUNDER_QUEUE.md` — "Branch protection
# needs GitHub Pro"). Added now anyway because it is the part of V2 §5's ask
# that costs nothing and needs no upgrade, and it documents the boundary both
# lanes have already been keeping by convention all session — so the rule is
# written down once branch protection can reference it, rather than invented
# from scratch at that point.
#
# Last matching pattern wins, so more specific paths are listed after the
# general ones they narrow.

# RCC — client
/apps/ @lawmind

# LCC — server
/services/ @lawmind
/packages/ @lawmind
/scripts/ @lawmind
/.github/ @lawmind

# Shared, either lane may touch with the other's awareness — not a hard
# boundary the way apps/** and services/** are.
/docs/ @lawmind
